Icons
-----

`ponytail/icon.png` and `ponytail/icon-dark.png` are original to this
repository. An earlier revision borrowed the Code-category icon bundled with
the MiniMax Code desktop application; that is no longer the case, and the
borrowed artwork is not redistributed here.

The mark is a single tapered stroke — a tied knot at the top, three rung
dashes, a long sweep that thins to a point. The taper is the argument: the
laziness ladder shortens at every rung until only the minimum is left. Both
variants are the same shape recoloured, generated at 512×512 RGBA with
transparent rounded corners to match the other icons in the Code category.

Why this file is separate
-------------------------

GitHub classifies a repository's license by fuzzy-matching the root `LICENSE`
against the SPDX corpus. Appending this notice to `LICENSE` pushed the match
below the detection threshold, so the repository displayed as "Other" instead
of MIT. Keeping `LICENSE` as unmodified SPDX text and the attributions here
lets automated license tooling read the terms correctly while the credit
stays visible to people. Nothing is dropped by the split.
